# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Chappter — Environment Variables
#
# NONE OF THESE ARE REQUIRED TO RUN THE APP. Demo Mode is on by default —
# `npm install && npm run dev` launches straight into a fully mocked chapter
# (no Clerk account, no backend, no database) with realistic sample data.
# See docs/DEMO_MODE.md.
#
# Only fill this in if you're reconnecting the real backend (set
# VITE_DEMO_MODE=false below first). Copy this file to .env.
# Never commit .env to version control.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# Set to "false" to disable Demo Mode and use real Clerk auth + the Express
# backend. Leave unset (or "true") for Demo Mode — the default.
# VITE_DEMO_MODE="false"

# Required only when VITE_DEMO_MODE=false.
# Found in Clerk Dashboard → API Keys
VITE_CLERK_PUBLISHABLE_KEY="pk_test_..."

# Required only when VITE_DEMO_MODE=false.
# Your machine's LAN IP address — NOT localhost (won't work on a physical
# device connected over Expo Go). Find it via System Settings → Network
# (macOS) or `ipconfig` (Windows).
VITE_API_URL="http://192.168.1.x:4000/api/v1"

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Backend CORS (only when VITE_DEMO_MODE=false)
#
# The web app runs on a different origin from the API (localhost:5173 vs
# localhost:4000), so the browser enforces CORS — which the mobile app never
# had to satisfy. backend/server.ts already reads CORS_ORIGIN; set it in
# backend/.env to the web app's origin:
#
#   CORS_ORIGIN="http://localhost:5173"
#
# In production it must list the deployed web origin — the server refuses to
# start in production without it.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
